{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["It shall be upon Aharon's forehead, that Aharon may bear the iniquity of the sacred gifts, etc. — according to its plain sense: Scripture is not speaking of the impurity of sacred gifts. Rather, this is its meaning: all the offerings that Israel bring — whether burnt offering or sin offering or guilt offering, to make atonement for them — the tzitz assists together with the offering, to bring it to remembrance before the Holy One, blessed be He, so that it be favorably accepted and a remembrance for the children of Israel, to make atonement for them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:31.297721875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}